{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-TMP-009", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF-TMP-009 | Study family SF-TMP-009: PULL_UP exposure-effect diagnostics\n- observed_research_question: PULL_UP exposure-effect diagnostics\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: The PULL_UP-specific decline with exposure is defensive adaptation rather than shooter selection/lineup artifact.\n- observed_result: With lineup FE: slope holding shot fixed -0.0255 (0.0061); shooter's earlier scored -0.1044 vs not scored +0.0693. No lineup FE: -0.0063 (0.0036); placebo other play types -0.0075 (0.0017).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: Effect shrinks from -0.0255 to -0.0063 without lineup FE and the same-shooter placebo on other play types is -0.0071/-0.0075, consistent with shooter-level confound.\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: artifact_found"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-TMP-012", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF-TMP-012 | Study family SF-TMP-012: Tail/null-model audit of the published suppression excess\n- observed_research_question: Tail/null-model audit of the published suppression excess\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: The published suppression excess (trigger drop minus matched control drop) exceeds appropriate null models and is asymmetric between decline and improvement tails.\n- observed_result: Reproduced excess 0.4080 CI [0.378,0.438]; G within-unit perm at 0.25: obs 0.3798 null 0.3744 resid +0.0054 z 0.40; asym neg-pos 0.0176 p 0.258; drift-centered tail mass ratio 1.007.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:drift\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:insufficient_exposure\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-TMP-001"}, {"id": "FAM:SF09", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF09 | Study family SF09: Double-suppression stacking (POST_UP then PUTBACK)\n- observed_research_question: Double-suppression stacking (POST_UP then PUTBACK)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Opponent POST_UP then PUTBACK stacks additively against the next star possession.\n- observed_result: [APPA-057] Baseline 1.210 n=960,764. After PUTBACK only 1.097 d=-0.113 n=15,898. After POST_UP only 1.091 d=-0.119 n=76,329. Stacked 1.138 d=-0.071 n=1,047 vs additive prediction -0.232. Mitchell after PUTBACK 0.919 vs 1 [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- observed_result: [APPS-042] POST_UP Q1->Q4 -0.065 (Q1 -0.119 to Q4 -0.184); PUTBACK -0.374 (0.144 to -0.23). TRANSITION cluster gradient +0.075 (unexpected vs hypothesized flat). Stacked delta -0.071 vs additive prediction -0.232 (less t [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: none (no failure recorded)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:implementation_bug\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:IMPLEMENTATION_BUG"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-TMP-021", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF-TMP-021 | Study family SF-TMP-021: Penalty-state adaptation (Pilot A)\n- observed_research_question: Penalty-state adaptation (Pilot A)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Behavior changes when the defense enters the penalty (3->4 team fouls).\n- observed_result: any_fta 3->4 -0.151 vs placebos -5.556/-9.655; rim_pct +0.015 vs +1.666/+2.077; pts +0.020.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: Penalty contrast not distinct from placebo contrasts; SEs not printed (sqrt warning).\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: TMP-021: 'with clock>2:30, game x offense x period fe; 2->3 and 4->5+ placebos. any_fta 3->4 -0.151 vs placebos -5.556/-9.655; rim_pct +0'\n- observed_method: Possessions with clock>2:30, game x offense x period FE; 2->3 and 4->5+ placebos.\n- observed_verdict: null\n- observed_failure_type: E_unclear"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
